# host/audren: give the audio producer a real-time deadline (time-constraint policy for the render thread)
#
# Upstream:  https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/commit/2edad1828de247aaf46c53cb288357cb65e84be0  (fixes #3059)
# Author:    seedds, 2026-11-20 19:57:44 +0800
# Co-authors:
#   Co-authored-by: nichq50
# Licence:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds (nxnative LICENSE); the attribution above is kept as the licence asks.
#
# WHAT IT CHANGES FOR THE PHONE
#   The in-process audio renderer's thread (render_main) asked for interactive QoS only. A QoS class is a priority, not a deadline: under load or a thermal clamp (the Ocarina log had
#   thermal state 2) the 5 ms refill can wake late and drain the output although mixing takes 0.07 ms (upstream #3059). After the output is set up the thread now declares
#   THREAD_TIME_CONSTRAINT_POLICY (period 5 ms, computation 1 ms, constraint 5 ms, preemptible) and restores the standard policy before the output is closed. A rejected request is logged
#   ("[RED] audren: render thread time-constraint policy ... failed to set") and playback goes on as before; 0401's 4.5 ms pacing is kept. Success line:
#   "audren: render thread time-constraint policy (requested period 5 ms, computation 1 ms) set (0)". Default ON; DM_AUDREN_RT=0 (game env.txt) keeps the default policy (A/B test).
#   Upstream states iOS runtime and power are NOT verified: the first device run must show whether iOS grants the policy to this thread.
#
# HAND-MERGED: one hunk (NX2Apple 0048 rewrote the end of render_main; the reset goes just after the render loop, before that teardown).
# RISK: low-medium. NOT run on a device. Shader chain id untouched.
#
# Apply with: patch -p1, to the tree out-stage/out-engine/engine + engine-patches/0401..0415 (0401 precedes it in hle_audren.c) and the candidates numbered below this one.

# REVISION 2 (2026-11-21, review L7): DM_AUDREN_RT is read by dm/host/dm_envflag.h (added by engine-patches/0415, which this patch now needs before it): 0 / off / false / no keep
#   the default policy, 1 / on / true / yes (and unset) set it; before, atoi() made "on" or "yes" turn it OFF. A value that is neither is logged and the policy is set.
#   t_audren_layout checks "Off" (opt-out) and "on" (policy set) besides "0".
--- a/dm/host/hle_audren.c
+++ b/dm/host/hle_audren.c
@@ -14,6 +14,10 @@
